    {
      "id": "deb_20260809120000_0001",
      "parentId": null,
      "authorProfileId": "profile-alice",
      "sourcePostId": "social-post-ai",
      "from": "Alice",
      "to": null,
      "start": "other",
      "confidence": "82",
      "antiReaction": true,
      "intention": "explore",
      "theme": "economy-tech",
      "title": "Does AI transform human creativity?",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "id": "d1",
          "text": "Creativity: the ability to produce new and useful ideas."
        },
        {
          "id": "d2",
          "text": "Generative AI: a model capable of producing content from examples."
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "text": "In 2025, 38% of creative studios used AI in their production pipeline."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "text": "AI tools reduced the average time required for visual prototyping by 30%."
        }
      ],
      "content": [
        "Generative AI can now produce text, images, and sound at unprecedented speed.",
        "The question is whether it amplifies human creativity or gradually replaces it."
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "author": "Bob",
          "confidence": 68,
          "title": "AI is already changing creative business models",
          "replyTo": "p1",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "id": "p2-1",
              "text": "Studios use AI to reduce costs, which can undermine human creators."
            },
            {
              "id": "p2-2",
              "text": "However, AI also opens new markets, particularly for independent creators."
            }
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "p3",
              "author": "Clara",
              "confidence": 61,
              "title": "Reducing costs is not always a bad thing",
              "replyTo": "p2-1",
              "paragraphs": [
                {
                  "id": "p3-1",
                  "text": "Lower costs can make it possible to fund more creative projects."
                },
                {
                  "id": "p3-2",
                  "text": "But that depends on how the savings are distributed."
                }
              ],
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "id": "p4",
              "author": "Dan",
              "confidence": 57,
              "title": "Independent creators benefit most from AI tools",
              "replyTo": "p2-2",
              "paragraphs": [
                {
                  "id": "p4-1",
                  "text": "AI tools let solo creators produce at the scale of a small studio."
                },
                {
                  "id": "p4-2",
                  "text": "This partly rebalances the playing field with larger organizations."
                }
              ],
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "id": "p5",
              "author": "Eva",
              "confidence": 70,
              "title": "The overall impact depends on the ethical framework",
              "replyTo": "p2",
              "paragraphs": [
                {
                  "id": "p5-1",
                  "text": "AI can be beneficial when governed by clear rules."
                },
                {
                  "id": "p5-2",
                  "text": "Without regulation, it may deepen inequalities in creative work."
                }
              ],
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p6",
          "author": "Fred",
          "confidence": 74,
          "title": "AI speeds things up but does not replace human intuition",
          "replyTo": "p1-1",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "id": "p6-1",
              "text": "Generation speed does not replace the human ability to form an intention."
            },
            {
              "id": "p6-2",
              "text": "AI remains dependent on existing data, which limits its originality."
            }
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "p8",
              "author": "Alice",
              "confidence": 85,
                  "title": "Human intention remains central",
              "replyTo": "p6-1",
              "paragraphs": [
                {
                  "id": "p8-1",
                      "text": "You are right: AI has no intention of its own; it only executes."
                },
                {
                  "id": "p8-2",
                      "text": "But it can amplify human intention by quickly exploring variations."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p9",
                  "author": "Fred",
                  "confidence": 76,
                  "title": "Rapid exploration changes how we create",
                  "replyTo": "p8",
                  "paragraphs": [
                    {
                      "id": "p9-1",
                      "text": "Faster exploration makes it possible to test more ideas in less time."
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "p9-2",
                      "text": "But it can also encourage quantity over depth."
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p7",
          "author": "Gina",
          "confidence": 72,
          "title": "AI can replace some tasks, but not vision",
          "replyTo": "p1-2",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "id": "p7-1",
              "text": "Repetitive or technical tasks can be automated easily."
            },
            {
              "id": "p7-2",
              "text": "But an overall artistic vision remains deeply human."
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "p10",
          "author": "Alice",
          "confidence": 88,
          "title": "Clarification sur la redistribution des gains",
          "replyTo": "p3",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "id": "p10-1",
              "text": "Clara, you raise an essential point about redistribution."
            },
            {
              "id": "p10-2",
              "text": "The problem is that creators do not always benefit from the savings."
            }
          ],
          "children": []
